From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:42:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/79] flashnext_mia: open through f212's CUDA family contract

TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE=mia now opens her family with native/cuda.zig's openWith, as every registry
family opens, instead of her own host:

- max_segments 1, prompt_rows 2048; Options take segments/slide (ignored), lanes (--parallel),
  kv8 (--kv-cache fp8, her --kv-dtype fp8), a nullable master and prompt_cache_gib.
- stream_bytes 0: her engine admits each request's window on its own sequence budget, so the
  server serves --parallel streams and reserves nothing per stream.
- The prompt cache is snap_* over Loaded.target (her lanes), lookahead 0; snap_ready leaves the
  store her budget (a quarter of the sequences' memory, 16 GiB at most, or --prompt-cache-gib;
  none on rank 1, which follows rank 0's notes).
- open refuses a null kernel set (f212's own glue): she replays a captured Triton set only;
  explain words that and her other open refusals.
- contextCeiling is her YaRN window, placementWeightBytes a rank's share of the files, benchmark
  her rank count. --vision and --slide are refused by f212's family refusals.
